tter\"?" :question/worked-solution "There are $3$ fillings to arrange, so there are $3!$ ways of arranging them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3! & =3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe order \"bacon, then jelly, then peanut butter\" is one of them. By subtracting $1$ from $6,$ we find the number of the filling arrangements that can be formed beside \"bacon, then jelly, then peanut butter\".\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bf5203bc-5ab0-5589-a556-b9d7b8e10dd7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bf5203bc-5ab0-5589-a556-b9d7b8e10dd7" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf5203bc-5ab0-5589-a556-b9d7b8e10dd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b35b872f-dd08-5fa3-9882-9d8c16329105" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c23ffa30-efbb-5616-8770-9cacaac1a764" "answer-b35b872f-dd08-5fa3-9882-9d8c16329105" "answer-16073d03-8af9-5352-8694-fd0e7a7a2373" "answer-0af6444e-1c3b-53bc-86a5-6ca247977195" "answer-4530975a-6b6e-57e2-ac4a-5c0253f6fdf7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c23ffa30-efbb-5616-8770-9cacaac1a764" :answer/id #uuid "c23ffa30-efbb-5616-8770-9cacaac1a764" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b35b872f-dd08-5fa3-9882-9d8c16329105" :answer/id #uuid "b35b872f-dd08-5fa3-9882-9d8c16329105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16073d03-8af9-5352-8694-fd0e7a7a2373" :answer/id #uuid "16073d03-8af9-5352-8694-fd0e7a7a2373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0af6444e-1c3b-53bc-86a5-6ca247977195" :answer/id #uuid "0af6444e-1c3b-53bc-86a5-6ca247977195" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4530975a-6b6e-57e2-ac4a-5c0253f6fdf7" :answer/id #uuid "4530975a-6b6e-57e2-ac4a-5c0253f6fdf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083458 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "activity-ebaef1eb-8213-50ec-b073-520ce6726e48" :activity/id #uuid "ebaef1eb-8213-50ec-b073-520ce6726e48" :activity/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050741 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-ad21cebd-ff8a-53c9-8283-5bf14acbfeb4" "step-6b903eb3-9061-58c8-98af-eddd22cd198a" "step-782ae1f7-abc5-5329-91db-e3c692dbda3d" "step-9ac80efa-ba10-5ae6-8679-cb450b1b7cff" "step-c2db6780-c7da-52ab-bdc1-0dd0e5f57833"] :activity/first-step "step-ad21cebd-ff8a-53c9-8283-5bf14acbfeb4" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ad21cebd-ff8a-53c9-8283-5bf14acbfeb4" :step/id #uuid "ad21cebd-ff8a-53c9-8283-5bf14acbfeb4" :step/content 17592186435475 :step/next "step-6b903eb3-9061-58c8-98af-eddd22cd198a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6b903eb3-9061-58c8-98af-eddd22cd198a" :step/id #uuid "6b903eb3-9061-58c8-98af-eddd22cd198a" :step/content 17592186435469 :step/next "step-782ae1f7-abc5-5329-91db-e3c692dbda3d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-782ae1f7-abc5-5329-91db-e3c692dbda3d" :step/id #uuid "782ae1f7-abc5-5329-91db-e3c692dbda3d" :step/content 17592186444169 :step/next "step-9ac80efa-ba10-5ae6-8679-cb450b1b7cff" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9ac80efa-ba10-5ae6-8679-cb450b1b7cff" :step/id #uuid "9ac80efa-ba10-5ae6-8679-cb450b1b7cff" :step/content 17592186435473 :step/next "step-c2db6780-c7da-52ab-bdc1-0dd0e5f57833" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c2db6780-c7da-52ab-bdc1-0dd0e5f57833" :step/id #uuid "c2db6780-c7da-52ab-bdc1-0dd0e5f57833" :step/content 17592186435471 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083311 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3cd87003-8b3d-5e51-bfe0-aa7c92e7f7e1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083221 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-859b5680-eb9f-5faf-a3e0-6d7891dc3557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083022 :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n_{n}P_r = \\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $20$ employees, so $n=20.$ We want to select $4$ of those employees to fill the roles of president, vice president, treasurer, and secretary, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to fill the roles is\n\n![](images/1a/1ae525b0e04502c3c1f4c8eb4ffd01419c48cbde67cbd721ad58300dc2f0ebb1.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3cd87003-8b3d-5e51-bfe0-aa7c92e7f7e1" :question/id #uuid "3cd87003-8b3d-5e51-bfe0-aa7c92e7f7e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-122214" :question/problem "${}_{20}{P}_{5}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=20$ and $r=5$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{20}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{20!}{(20-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20!}{15!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18\\cdot 17\\cdot 16\\cdot \\cancel{15!}}{\\cancel{15!}} \\\\  & =20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18\\cdot 17\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =1\\,860\\,480.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7e4a1ba6-7426-5a33-ab15-d55e1bd0f323"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7e4a1ba6-7426-5a33-ab15-d55e1bd0f323" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e4a1ba6-7426-5a33-ab15-d55e1bd0f323" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-18a16957-8346-51b2-8f15-6a1a2ff9a2a9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c0888d94-3576-5d80-b4b7-c1a0f50ff127" "answer-6ed50362-0918-5cd9-a37b-fcc0e0d54a09" "answer-18a16957-8346-51b2-8f15-6a1a2ff9a2a9" "answer-620cf998-2ccb-5238-9df9-af34228d14fb" "answer-8503f27d-4211-57a3-b8ee-c3773041176b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0888d94-3576-5d80-b4b7-c1a0f50ff127" :answer/id #uuid "c0888d94-3576-5d80-b4b7-c1a0f50ff127" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "109\\,440" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ed50362-0918-5cd9-a37b-fcc0e0d54a09" :answer/id #uuid "6ed50362-0918-5cd9-a37b-fcc0e0d54a09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "116\\,280" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18a16957-8346-51b2-8f15-6a1a2ff9a2a9" :answer/id #uuid "18a16957-8346-51b2-8f15-6a1a2ff9a2a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,860\\,480" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-620cf998-2ccb-5238-9df9-af34228d14fb" :answer/id #uuid "620cf998-2ccb-5238-9df9-af34228d14fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "93\\,024" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8503f27d-4211-57a3-b8ee-c3773041176b" :answer/id #uuid "8503f27d-4211-57a3-b8ee-c3773041176b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "97\\,920" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-859b5680-eb9f-5faf-a3e0-6d7891dc3557" :question/id #uuid "859b5680-eb9f-5faf-a3e0-6d7891dc3557" :question/math-academy-id "q-122230" :question/problem "A cook designs a menu for his restaurant from Thursday to Sunday. Each day, only one main dish will be served, and it will not be repeated on any other day. If the cook wants to choose from the $9$ most popular dishes, how many different menus can the cook design?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $9$ popular dishes to choose from, so $n=9.$ We want to select $4$ of those for the menu, one for each day (Thursday, Friday, Saturday, and Sunday), so we have $r=4.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{9}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{9!}{(9-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9!}{5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3\\,024.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a1de2e92-9b96-54c1-839b-6cad9c1cd05b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1de2e92-9b96-54c1-839b-6cad9c1cd05b" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1de2e92-9b96-54c1-839b-6cad9c1cd05b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95fe5149-ddb8-5382-98ba-baf63aff6f61" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c4e95ae-1f65-52fc-a331-c1749918a60a" "answer-d7093da7-6fca-5b2f-bf9a-07216a1b922e" "answer-8360580c-95af-5b20-92d1-a7013c63af4a" "answer-95fe5149-ddb8-5382-98ba-baf63aff6f61" "answer-899595e7-00db-59d9-81ef-b12f0f1dd138"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c4e95ae-1f65-52fc-a331-c1749918a60a" :answer/id #uuid "6c4e95ae-1f65-52fc-a331-c1749918a60a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7093da7-6fca-5b2f-bf9a-07216a1b922e" :answer/id #uuid "d7093da7-6fca-5b2f-bf9a-07216a1b922e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,260" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8360580c-95af-5b20-92d1-a7013c63af4a" :answer/id #uuid "8360580c-95af-5b20-92d1-a7013c63af4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "336" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95fe5149-ddb8-5382-98ba-baf63aff6f61" :answer/id #uuid "95fe5149-ddb8-5382-98ba-baf63aff6f61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,024" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-899595e7-00db-59d9-81ef-b12f0f1dd138" :answer/id #uuid "899595e7-00db-59d9-81ef-b12f0f1dd138" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,561" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186084471 :tutorial/content "In general, the number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n_{n}P_r = \\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\n$$\n\nIn the previous example, we had $n=5$ books and $r=3$ slots in the bookshelf. Using the formula, the total number of permutations is computed as\n![](images/3d/3d53f73ea9e1a5d0966237c002f2d11075ee10d519bb6a2823b2ff0fea8c8e53.svg)\n\nWe got the same result as before!\n\n**Note:** We can write ${}_nP_r$ in a number of ways:\n\n$$\n{}_nP_r = {}^nP_r = P(n,r)\n$$\n\nAll of these mean the same thing." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083409 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068750 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-940f3759-8774-576e-891c-0f76989295c4" "question-d2b7c3bc-8988-5881-96d5-877a27dfd407" "question-d718b4fe-ac83-5ded-9cff-9bf61a11c436"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-940f3759-8774-576e-891c-0f76989295c4" :question/id #uuid "940f3759-8774-576e-891c-0f76989295c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-14194" :question/problem "Find $p$ if $-2$ is a root of $f(x)=5{x}^{2}+6x-2p.$" :question/worked-solution "Since  $x=-2$ is a root, we have $f(-2)=0.$ Therefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=-2,$ set it equal to $0,$ and solve the equation for the parameter $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)^{2}+6(-2)-2p & =0 \\\\ 20-12-2p & =0 \\\\ 8-2p & =0 \\\\ -2p & =-8 \\\\ p & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a0a44b2-6e7c-58bd-8a08-7b91d747ebd4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a0a44b2-6e7c-58bd-8a08-7b91d747ebd4" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a0a44b2-6e7c-58bd-8a08-7b91d747ebd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-16c11ec4-ff0c-5c06-86de-a5fdbf8b9db1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a670b93b-9bea-55ed-97fc-24e49d5de5cd" "answer-2bc0013d-319f-5abd-b000-4099afd2ca7d" "answer-027f0819-c021-5635-b7d1-21f53a81eb36" "answer-16c11ec4-ff0c-5c06-86de-a5fdbf8b9db1" "answer-c210b6d6-4799-5836-860c-3d8f72c0f36e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a670b93b-9bea-