swer-field/choices ["answer-c0f443c9-ef17-58cc-b95a-61015c8b0bb9" "answer-5b8d9c69-c461-5657-b7db-55fc0f95502c" "answer-ed36e04c-50f8-5707-a26d-cd2bff039d69" "answer-49d51132-3a98-5562-997b-c3804fe69000" "answer-63e5a07e-8754-5577-bdb4-5151751ade2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0f443c9-ef17-58cc-b95a-61015c8b0bb9" :answer/id #uuid "c0f443c9-ef17-58cc-b95a-61015c8b0bb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.06" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b8d9c69-c461-5657-b7db-55fc0f95502c" :answer/id #uuid "5b8d9c69-c461-5657-b7db-55fc0f95502c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.125" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed36e04c-50f8-5707-a26d-cd2bff039d69" :answer/id #uuid "ed36e04c-50f8-5707-a26d-cd2bff039d69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49d51132-3a98-5562-997b-c3804fe69000" :answer/id #uuid "49d51132-3a98-5562-997b-c3804fe69000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63e5a07e-8754-5577-bdb4-5151751ade2e" :answer/id #uuid "63e5a07e-8754-5577-bdb4-5151751ade2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.375" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-92bd4292-ffa2-5865-9aeb-f65630d4d79e" :question/id #uuid "92bd4292-ffa2-5865-9aeb-f65630d4d79e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105986" :question/problem "Given that $P(L|K)=0.6,$ $P(K)=0.4,$ and $P(L)=0.5,$ compute $P(K|L).$" :question/worked-solution "Using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(K|L) & =\\frac{P(L|K)P(K)}{P(L)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.6)(0.4)}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.24}{0.5} \\\\  & =0.48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-62d78285-4735-549a-a2a2-a216659cea42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-62d78285-4735-549a-a2a2-a216659cea42" :answer-field/id #uuid "62d78285-4735-549a-a2a2-a216659cea42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-04ab9885-0e91-5abb-84cb-80ed9e925c3b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4b61d2fb-e8ee-5f41-859c-bbe3bd0c7e05" "answer-5f4f5e33-ab5c-5cb3-81f8-7a9441f7a1fb" "answer-7f73b3a0-023a-530f-a586-a916f7f3a52b" "answer-04ab9885-0e91-5abb-84cb-80ed9e925c3b" "answer-790602f9-2626-58ac-bded-d74954f23b2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b61d2fb-e8ee-5f41-859c-bbe3bd0c7e05" :answer/id #uuid "4b61d2fb-e8ee-5f41-859c-bbe3bd0c7e05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f4f5e33-ab5c-5cb3-81f8-7a9441f7a1fb" :answer/id #uuid "5f4f5e33-ab5c-5cb3-81f8-7a9441f7a1fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f73b3a0-023a-530f-a586-a916f7f3a52b" :answer/id #uuid "7f73b3a0-023a-530f-a586-a916f7f3a52b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04ab9885-0e91-5abb-84cb-80ed9e925c3b" :answer/id #uuid "04ab9885-0e91-5abb-84cb-80ed9e925c3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-790602f9-2626-58ac-bded-d74954f23b2a" :answer/id #uuid "790602f9-2626-58ac-bded-d74954f23b2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-062302ea-c279-555c-ae6b-c50720d77be2" :question/id #uuid "062302ea-c279-555c-ae6b-c50720d77be2" :question/math-academy-id "q-105982" :question/problem "Given that $P(F|G)=0.5,$ $P(F)=0.25,$ and $P(G)=0.3,$ compute $P(G|F).$" :question/worked-solution "Using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G|F) & =\\frac{P(F|G)P(G)}{P(F)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.5)(0.3)}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.15}{0.25} \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd54b5e5-f0c2-5a3b-a450-ecfed249f990"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd54b5e5-f0c2-5a3b-a450-ecfed249f990" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd54b5e5-f0c2-5a3b-a450-ecfed249f990" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d887ea2d-dd53-5179-8bad-72136235d1fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a7135b37-f0fd-5ed4-9743-47c5e79c9779" "answer-dff0f50c-6fe1-5583-ad75-f9fff5c8fb84" "answer-de268d17-6d3c-5965-b7bb-48ce861426fc" "answer-d887ea2d-dd53-5179-8bad-72136235d1fc" "answer-e489e907-0fe1-5ad7-8dec-8d7f7c5da294"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7135b37-f0fd-5ed4-9743-47c5e79c9779" :answer/id #uuid "a7135b37-f0fd-5ed4-9743-47c5e79c9779" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dff0f50c-6fe1-5583-ad75-f9fff5c8fb84" :answer/id #uuid "dff0f50c-6fe1-5583-ad75-f9fff5c8fb84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de268d17-6d3c-5965-b7bb-48ce861426fc" :answer/id #uuid "de268d17-6d3c-5965-b7bb-48ce861426fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d887ea2d-dd53-5179-8bad-72136235d1fc" :answer/id #uuid "d887ea2d-dd53-5179-8bad-72136235d1fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e489e907-0fe1-5ad7-8dec-8d7f7c5da294" :answer/id #uuid "e489e907-0fe1-5ad7-8dec-8d7f7c5da294" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7838b043-50f3-55a8-b1f4-349f8ab97093" :question/id #uuid "7838b043-50f3-55a8-b1f4-349f8ab97093" :question/math-academy-id "q-170679" :question/problem "On an MLB team, $75%$ of all players are American citizens. It is known that $15%$ of them also speak Spanish, while $25%$ of all players on the team speak Spanish. If a player who speaks Spanish is randomly selected for a TV interview, what is the probability that he is American? Express your answer as a percentage." :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the event that the randomly selected player is American, and let $S$ be the event that a player speaks Spanish. Then, we require $P(A|S),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(A|S)=\\frac{P(S|A)P(A)}{P(S)}\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- $P(S|A)=0.15,$ since $15%$ of all American players on the team speak spanish.\n\n- $P(A)=0.75,$ since $0.75%$ of the players on the team are American citizens.\n\n- $P(S)=0.25,$ since  $25%$ of all players on the team speak Spanish.\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A|S) & =\\frac{P(S|A)P(A)}{P(S)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.15)(0.75)}{0.25} \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-87d6bcc7-6589-5e99-bac2-8e50a7a34102"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-87d6bcc7-6589-5e99-bac2-8e50a7a34102" :answer-field/id #uuid "87d6bcc7-6589-5e99-bac2-8e50a7a34102" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-173c78ca-07cd-5a6c-9761-ea787464b15a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3aa84135-60de-5943-b3d5-5a014c50188d" "answer-9aa85b33-9082-59e6-8111-8fff5a6185df" "answer-2657e280-a097-5f1b-91d1-d15ac0d109bc" "answer-173c78ca-07cd-5a6c-9761-ea787464b15a" "answer-b7316c1e-431c-5433-ad77-0aabc09e351b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3aa84135-60de-5943-b3d5-5a014c50188d" :answer/id #uuid "3aa84135-60de-5943-b3d5-5a014c50188d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9aa85b33-9082-59e6-8111-8fff5a6185df" :answer/id #uuid "9aa85b33-9082-59e6-8111-8fff5a6185df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2657e280-a097-5f1b-91d1-d15ac0d109bc" :answer/id #uuid "2657e280-a097-5f1b-91d1-d15ac0d109bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-173c78ca-07cd-5a6c-9761-ea787464b15a" :answer/id #uuid "173c78ca-07cd-5a6c-9761-ea787464b15a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7316c1e-431c-5433-ad77-0aabc09e351b" :answer/id #uuid "b7316c1e-431c-5433-ad77-0aabc09e351b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "47%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4fe71dad-9ede-5ba8-b760-d7b3b5dd3ac6" :question/id #uuid "4fe71dad-9ede-5ba8-b760-d7b3b5dd3ac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42569" :question/problem "On a particular industrial estate, the probability of smoke on a given day is $10%$ and the probability of a dangerous fire is $1.5%.$ It is known that $90%$ of dangerous fires create smoke. What is the probability of a dangerous fire when there is smoke? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $S$ be the event that there is smoke, and let $F$ be the event that there is a dangerous fire. Then, we require $P(F|S),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(F|S)=\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S)}\n$$\n\n- $P(S)=0.1,$ since the probability of smoke is $10%.$\n\n- $P(F)=0.015,$ since the probability of dangerous fire is $1.5%.$\n\n- $P(S|F)=0.9,$ since  $90%$ of dangerous fires make smoke.\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|S) & =\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.9\\cdot 0.015}{0.1} \\\\  & ≈0.14,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57bdf9d4-8e50-5968-9900-6c66def0225d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57bdf9d4-8e50-5968-9900-6c66def0225d" :answer-field/id #uuid "57bdf9d4-8e50-5968-9900-6c66def0225d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ab42b52-3ca2-50ff-8c28-d4a3662f6586" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5be87e40-3750-5117-b4cd-0091a8b0ae50" "answer-9e8f44d0-fe3f-5ff0-81df-53d7daed0469" "answer-9ab42b52-3ca2-50ff-8c28-d4a3662f6586" "answer-9360a81e-537b-5ac8-a6f0-68bd41ed97d0" "answer-cafe4a0b-7ce5-53c1-b61a-7bd7d7990f17"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5be87e40-3750-5117-b4cd-0091a8b0ae50" :answer/id #uuid "5be87e40-3750-5117-b4cd-0091a8b0ae50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.01" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e8f44d0-fe3f-5ff0-81df-53d7daed0469" :answer/id #uuid "9e8f44d0-fe3f-5ff0-81df-53d7daed0469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ab42b52-3ca2-50ff-8c28-d4a3662f6586" :answer/id #uuid "9ab42b52-3ca2-50ff-8c28-d4a3662f6586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9360a81e-537b-5ac8-a6f0-68bd41ed97d0" :answer/id #uuid "9360a81e-537b-5ac8-a6f0-68bd41ed97d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cafe4a0b-7ce5-53c1-b61a-7bd7d7990f17" :answer/id #uuid "cafe4a0b-7ce5-53c1-b61a-7bd7d7990f17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-74a09e82-c6f4-5ba5-932c-01b4112c68fd" :question/id #uuid "74a09e82-c6f4-5ba5-932c-01b4112c68fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-170678" :question/problem "At a soccer game, $60%$ of the spectators are men. It is known that $20%$ of the men in the crowd are over $50,$ while $30%$ of all people in the crowd are over $50.$ If a person over $50$ is picked at random from the crowd, what is the probability that the person will be a man?" :question/worked-solution "Let $M$ be the event that the randomly selected person is a man, and let $F$ be the event that it is over $50.$ Then, we require $P(M|F),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(M|F)=\\frac{P(F|M)P(M)}{P(F)}\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- $P(F|M)=0.2,$ since $20%$ of the men at the game are over $50.$\n\n- $P(M)=0.6,$ since $60%$ of all the spectators are men.\n\n- $P(F)=0.3,$ since $30%$ of all spectators are over $50.$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M|F) & =\\frac{P(F|M)P(M)}{P(F)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.2)(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fd74e72c-2c1f-53f8-8056-3995854a281c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fd74e72c-2c1f-53f8-8056-3995854a281c" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd74e72c-2c1f-53f8-8056-3995854a281c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b63be08a-971e-568a-bcf0-aa32ee85628f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6591953e-3f02-5704-a30f-7350a0937ed3" "answer-3e033aa6-4de7-5db1-800c-879f51bc96d1" "answer-e3413079-7aa5-56cc-86b6-cb2dc4f54f32" "answer-b63be08a-971e-568a-bcf0-aa32ee85628f" "answer-53c8eae7-65b6-5519-80c5-4696c5b5a043"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6591953e-3f02-5704-a30f-7350a0937ed3" :answer/id #uuid "6591953e-3f02-5704-a30f-7350a0937ed3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e033aa6-4de7-5db1-800c-879f51bc96d1" :answer/id #uuid "3e033aa6-4de7-5db1-800c-879f51bc96d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3413079-7aa5-56cc-86b6-cb2dc4f54f32" :answer/id #uuid "e3413079-7aa5-56cc-86b6-cb2dc4f54f32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b63be08a-971e-568a-bcf0-aa32ee85628f" :answer/id #uuid "b63be08a-971e-568a-bcf0-aa32ee85628f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53c8eae7-65b6-5519-80c5-4696c5b5a043" :answer/id #uuid "53c8eae7-65b6-5519-80c5-4696c5b5a043" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f5454beb-e917-5a8e-86e1-4e0232e2e094" :question/id #uuid "f5454beb-e917-5a8e-86e1-4e0232e2e094" :question/math-academy-id "q-170681" :question/problem "Two groups of high school students are competing in a math contest. Group $A$ consists of $5$ girls and $3$ boys, while Group $B$ consists of $2$ girls and $4$ boys. For the first challenge, one group is randomly selected, and one student is randomly selected from that group. If the selected student is a girl, what is the probability that she is from Group $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $B$ be the event that Group $B$ is selected, and let $G$ be the event that a randomly selected student is a girl. Then, we require $P(B|G),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(B|G)=\\frac{P(G|B)P(B)}{P(G)}=\\frac{P(G|B)P(B)}{P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|{B}^{′})P({B}^{′})}\n$$\n\nNote that ${B}^{′}$ is the event that Group A is selected.\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- Since Group $A$ consists of $5$ girls and $3$ boys and Group $B$ consists of $2$ girls and $4$ boys, we have\n\n$$\nP(G|B)=\\frac{2}{6}=\\frac{1}{3},\\,P(G|{B}^{′})=\\frac{5}{8}.\n$$\n\n- Since the group is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(B)=P({B}^{′})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(B|G) & =\\frac{P(G|B)P(B)}{P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|{B}^{′})P({B}^{′})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6})}{(\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{16})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6})}{(\\frac{23}{48})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{23}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed19dedc-ec19-5969-a25e-5d950eb640c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed19dedc-ec19-5969-a25e-5d950eb640c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed19dedc-ec19-5969-a25e-5d950eb640c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aa044da1-85a9-511d-b5d4-f73842833f10" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b9fdd295-7d5b-5a27-b880-407ff1f5f955" "answer-dcd04df4-f6d0-543d-b41f-3f62636bc031" "answer-08668600-cdfa-52f8-ab7a-d4a36c8ad7e8" "answer-aa044da1-85a9-511d-b5d4-f73842833f10" "answer-1ffc0230-8021-5fb9-97c8-3bdfd65c4744"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9fdd295-7d5b-5a27-b880-407ff1f5f955" :answer/id #uuid "b9fdd295-7d5b-5a27-b880-407ff1f5f955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcd04df4-f6d0-543d-b41f-3f62636bc031" :answer/id #uuid "dcd04df4-f6d0-543d-b41f-3f62636bc031" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08668600-cdfa-52f8-ab7a-d4a36c8ad7e8" :answer/id #uuid "08668600-cdfa-52f8-ab7a-d4a36c8ad7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa044da1-85a9-511d-b5d4-f73842833f10" :answer/id #uuid "aa044da1-85a9-511d-b5d4-f73842833f10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{23}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ffc0230-8021-5fb9-97c8-3bdfd65c4744" :answer/id #uuid "1ffc0230-8021-5fb9-97c8-3bdfd65c4744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{23}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d7bc91a9-28bf-5e94-8b54-f2a8632dbd6e" :question/id #uuid "d7bc91a9-28bf-5e94-8b54-f2a8632dbd6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106224" :question/problem "A survey of Bulgarian citizens showed that $17%$ of all females and  $38%$ of all males smoke. $51%$ of the population are female. If a smoker from this population is selected at random, what is the probability of them being female? Express your answer as a percentage to the nearest percent." :question/worked-solution "Let $S$ be the event that a randomly selected person smokes, and let $F$ be the event that they are female. Then, we require $P(F|S),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(F|S)=\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S)}=\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S|F)P(F)+P(S|{F}^{′})P({F}^{′})}\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- Since $17%$ of all females and  $38%$ of all males smoke, we have\n\n$$\nP(S|F)=0.17,\\,P(S|{F}^{′})=0.38.\n$$\n\n- Since $51%$ of the population are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.51,\\,P({F}^{′})=1-0.51=0.49.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|S) & =\\frac{P(S|F)P(F)}{P(S|F)P(F)+P(S|{F}^{′})P({F}^{′})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.17)(0.51)}{(0.17)(0.51)+(0.38)(0.49)} \\\\  & ≈32%\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest percent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e5cec0d0-a37e-5101-b62c-020ee35e0baf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e5cec0d0-a37e-5101-b62c-020ee35e0baf" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5cec0d0-a37e-5101-b62c-020ee35e0baf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f7095591-02a5-59b3-8d3e-ad153f388853" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23c9b185-7787-54a4-bca2-f16375591efa" "answer-f7095591-02a5-59b3-8d3e-ad153f388853" "answer-6a61f532-a319-545e-866c-fd70cd536703" "answer-02a70b8e-641b-5f9f-8429-083646503d5a" "answer-91283086-43e6-5966-9458-5ec5d404d381"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23c9b185-7787-54a4-bca2-f16375591efa" :answer/id #uuid "23c9b185-7787-54a4-bca2-f16375591efa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7095591-02a5-59b3-8d3e-ad153f388853" :answer/id #uuid "f7095591-02a5-59b3-8d3e-ad153f388853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a61f532-a319-545e-866c-fd70cd536703" :answer/id #uuid "6a61f532-a319-545e-866c-fd70cd536703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02a70b8e-641b-5f9f-8429-083646503d5a" :answer/id #uuid "02a70b8e-641b-5f9f-8429-083646503d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "34%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91283086-43e6-5966-9458-5ec5d404d381" :answer/id #uuid "91283086-43e6-5966-9458-5ec5d404d381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0ba278eb-bd8e-5c0e-8df1-e6e393201d18" :question/id #uuid "0ba278eb-bd8e-5c0e-8df1-e6e393201d18" :question/math-academy-id "q-106242" :question/problem "A survey of adult citizens of a particular city showed that $32%$ of all females and $5%$ of all males don't eat after $6$ p.m. $51%$ of the population are female. If a person who eats after $6$ p.m. is selected at random, what is the probability of them being male? Express your answer as a percentage to the nearest percent." :question/worked-solution "Let $E$ be the event that a randomly selected person eats after $6$ p.m., and let $M$ be the event that they are male. Then, we require $P(M|E),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(M|E)=\\frac{P(E|M)P(M)}{P(E)}=\\frac{P(E|M)P(M)}{P(E|M)P(M)+P(E|{M}^{′})P({M}^{′})}\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- Since $32%$ of all females and  $5%$ of all males don't eat after $6$ p.m, we have\n\n$$\nP(E|M)=1-0.05=0.95,\\,P(E|{M}^{′})=1-0.32=0.68.\n$$\n\n- Since $51%$ of the population are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(M)=1-0.51=0.49,\\,P({M}^{′})=0.51.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M|E) & =\\frac{P(E|M)P(M)}{P(E|M)P(M)+P(E|{M}^{′})P({M}^{′})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.95)(0.49)}{(0.95)(0.49)+(0.68)(0.51)} \\\\  & ≈57%\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest percent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59356800-2af7-5a74-9697-ca78c9e24c95"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59356800-2af7-5a74-9697-ca78c9e24c95" :answer-field/id #uuid "59356800-2af7-5a74-9697-ca78c9e24c95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-27163e64-ae56-5a01-ba08-3fcd6fa957eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7f159084-aaea-5881-b203-85398de327d4" "answer-18a6a22b-b44c-52f9-ad3e-8ce36c0c0333" "answer-27163e64-ae56-5a01-ba08-3fcd6fa957eb" "answer-572a21b4-bb72-5c4c-aba6-d9b8820f6a5f" "answer-45c30ff2-47a3-55bc-89c5-a3c9b9084fda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f159084-aaea-5881-b203-85398de327d4" :answer/id #uuid "7f159084-aaea-5881-b203-85398de327d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "55%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18a6a22b-b44c-52f9-ad3e-8ce36c0c0333" :answer/id #uuid "18a6a22b-b44c-52f9-ad3e-8ce36c0c0333" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "56%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27163e64-ae56-5a01-ba08-3fcd6fa957eb" :answer/id #uuid "27163e64-ae56-5a01-ba08-3fcd6fa957eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "57%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-572a21b4-bb72-5c4c-aba6-d9b8820f6a5f" :answer/id #uuid "572a21b4-bb72-5c4c-aba6-d9b8820f6a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "58%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45c30ff2-47a3-55bc-89c5-a3c9b9084fda" :answer/id #uuid "45c30ff2-47a3-55bc-89c5-a3c9b9084fda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "59%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d0b4bd1c-2214-5d30-8eda-6058d4c56287" :question/id #uuid "d0b4bd1c-2214-5d30-8eda-6058d4c56287" :question/math-academy-id "q-5787" :question/problem "A laboratory test for a particular disease is conducted on some patients. Of the tested patients, $95%$ of those infected and $4%$ of those not infected tested positive for the disease. Only $10%$ of the entire population is infected with the disease. What is the probability that a randomly chosen patient that tested positive is infected? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly chosen patient is infected with the disease, and let $T$ be the event they tested positive. Then, we require $P(D|T),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(D|T)=\\frac{P(T|D)P(D)}{P(T)}=\\frac{P(T|D)P(D)}{P(T|D)P(D)+P(T|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})}\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- Since the probability of an infected person testing positive is $95%,$ and the probability of a non-infected person testing positive is $4%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(T|D)=0.95,\\,P(T|{D}^{′})=0.04.\n$$\n\n- Since only $10%$ of the population has the disease, we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.1,\\,P({D}^{′})=1-0.1=0.9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D|T) & =\\frac{P(T|D)P(D)}{P(T|D)P(D)+P(T|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.95)(0.1)}{(0.95)(0.1)+(0.04)(0.9)} \\\\  & ≈0.73\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4f7d0a9-5a27-5459-8a96-37790d16d10f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4f7d0a9-5a27-5459-8a96-37790d16d10f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4f7d0a9-5a27-5459-8a96-37790d16d10f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f9ea11e2-7f1e-5b27-8a6d-549184b965b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87a0d937-2322-5709-8228-c8ba006d3f62" "answer-408436ae-fcb7-5192-bc36-9e3f0f7634c4" "answer-a67c16ed-d105-58e7-b006-7489ffd0523f" "answer-3307c114-ee95-5061-841e-9f5b1821a620" "answer-f9ea11e2-7f1e-5b27-8a6d-549184b965b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87a0d937-2322-5709-8228-c8ba006d3f62" :answer/id #uuid "87a0d937-2322-5709-8228-c8ba006d3f62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-408436ae-fcb7-5192-bc36-9e3f0f7634c4" :answer/id #uuid "408436ae-fcb7-5192-bc36-9e3f0f7634c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a67c16ed-d105-58e7-b006-7489ffd0523f" :answer/id #uuid "a67c16ed-d105-58e7-b006-7489ffd0523f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.67" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3307c114-ee95-5061-841e-9f5b1821a620" :answer/id #uuid "3307c114-ee95-5061-841e-9f5b1821a620" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9ea11e2-7f1e-5b27-8a6d-549184b965b0" :answer/id #uuid "f9ea11e2-7f1e-5b27-8a6d-549184b965b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.73" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-befc2ac4-e448-5384-bd13-1313e616793b" :question/id #uuid "befc2ac4-e448-5384-bd13-1313e616793b" :question/math-academy-id "q-5788" :question/problem "A laboratory test for a particular allergy is conducted on some patients. Of the tested patients, $96%$ of allergy sufferers and $3%$ of non-allergic patients tested positive for the allergy. Only $4%$ of the entire population has the allergy. What is the probability that a randomly chosen patient that tested positive is an allergy sufferer? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the event that a randomly chosen patient is an allergy sufferer, and let $T$ be the event they tested positive. Then, we require $P(A|T),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP(A|T)=\\frac{P(T|A)P(A)}{P(T)}=\\frac{P(T|A)P(A)}{P(T|A)P(A)+P(T|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})}\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- Since the probability of a person who has the allergy testing positive is $96%,$ and the probability of a non-allergic person testing positive is $3%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(T|A)=0.96,\\,P(T|{A}^{′})=0.03.\n$$\n\n- Since only $4%$ of the population suffers the allergy, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.04,\\,P({A}^{′})=1-0.04=0.96.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A|T) & =\\frac{P(T|A)P(A)}{P(T|A)P(A)+P(T|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.96)(0.04)}{(0.96)(0.04)+(0.03)(0.96)} \\\\  & ≈0.57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d1e98b60-187d-5aae-9ce2-daeaf5ade61f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d1e98b60-187d-5aae-9ce2-daeaf5ade61f" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1e98b60-187d-5aae-9ce2-daeaf5ade61f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c0111cfe-e353-588e-8af3-1ae79def79e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9ba81f0e-1c4e-5cdb-897c-d3bd7096b0fb" "answer-8c571f86-5a66-5e4e-a53f-a859152ee43f" "answer-23ce4d3b-cda1-5a8e-9672-c0c366c0eeeb" "answer-c0111cfe-e353-588e-8af3-1ae79def79e1" "answer-ff70f6bf-9c7a-558b-9578-7602758cd0bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ba81f0e-1c4e-5cdb-897c-d3bd7096b0fb" :answer/id #uuid "9ba81f0e-1c4e-5cdb-897c-d3bd7096b0fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c571f86-5a66-5e4e-a53f-a859152ee43f" :answer/id #uuid "8c571f86-5a66-5e4e-a53f-a859152ee43f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.47" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23ce4d3b-cda1-5a8e-9672-c0c366c0eeeb" :answer/id #uuid "23ce4d3b-cda1-5a8e-9672-c0c366c0eeeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0111cfe-e353-588e-8af3-1ae79def79e1" :answer/id #uuid "c0111cfe-e353-588e-8af3-1ae79def79e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.57" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff70f6bf-9c7a-558b-9578-7602758cd0bd" :answer/id #uuid "ff70f6bf-9c7a-558b-9578-7602758cd0bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-729d63e1-69ab-5f12-b423-6126fc288807" :question/id #uuid "729d63e1-69ab-5f12-b423-6126fc288807" :question/math-academy-id "q-106498" :question/problem "A laboratory test for a particular disease is conducted on some patients. Of the tested patients, $94%$ of those infected and $7%$ of those not infected tested positive for the disease. Only $12%$ of the entire population is infected with the disease. What is the probability that a randomly chosen patient that tested negative is not infected? Round your answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly chosen patient is infected with the disease, and let $T$ be the event they tested positive. Then, we require $P({D}^{′}|{T}^{′}),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem.\n\n$$\nP({D}^{′}|{T}^{′})=\\frac{P({T}^{′}|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})}{P({T}^{′})}=\\frac{P({T}^{′}|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})}{P({T}^{′}|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})+P({T}^{′}|D)P(D)}\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- Since the probability of an infected person testing positive is $94%,$ and the probability of a non-infected person testing positive is $7%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP({T}^{′}|D)=1-0.94=0.06,\\,P({T}^{′}|{D}^{′})=1-0.07=0.93.\n$$\n\n- Since only $12%$ of the population has the disease, we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.12\\,P({D}^{′})=1-0.12=0.88.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({D}^{′}|{T}^{′}) & =\\frac{P({T}^{′}|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})}{P({T}^{′}|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})+P({T}^{′}|D)P(D)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.93)(0.88)}{(0.93)(0.88)+(0.06)(0.12)} \\\\  & ≈0.9913\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb0df150-a742-5467-bdb9-d727d51505a7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb0df150-a742-5467-bdb9-d727d51505a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0df150-a742-5467-bdb9-d727d51505a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-26e742ea-5326-5b39-801a-a08dfb32c9e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-187c8520-6d60-5a7b-a412-938adbc2ec03" "answer-6dd21978-fd97-5670-80d0-583c75b3b9af" "answer-d860c886-503f-5d02-9030-15c830db168a" "answer-26e742ea-5326-5b39-801a-